3. AGENT FRAMEWORK / OSS FRONTIER

NEW =E2=80=94 Paper2Agent

What is new: automated conversion of scientific papers into AI agents.
Published in Nature on Sep 17, 2026.

Technical delta: instead of an agent merely retrieving/summarizing a
paper, the research artifact is transformed into an interactive agent
that exposes the paper=E2=80=99s methods/data/code as usable capability. Th=
e
publication also describes paper-agents interacting to support
discovery.

Why serious builders may use it: scientific tooling has unusually high
friction between reading a method and actually running/adapting it.
Packaging the method as an agent attacks that integration bottleneck
directly.

Route: Nature paper:
https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11044-y . Code/reproduction
status should be rechecked next run rather than inferred from
secondary snippets.

Trajectory inference: 6m: reproductions and domain-specific paper
agents; 18m: agent-callable research-method registries; 36m: papers
increasingly ship executable agent interfaces; 60m: scientific
literature partly behaves like a capability graph rather than a text
corpus.

Privately implication: a paper-agent is also a software supply-chain
object. If scientific methods become callable agents, Privately should
eventually be able to fingerprint the
code/data/tools/network/authority a paper-agent introduces before
allowing it into a research environment.

